cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these artifacts, please cite this repository and the accompanying manuscript."
title: "Data and Reproducibility Artifacts for: Evaluating AST-Derived Knowledge Graph Retrieval for AIOps Incident Diagnosis in Apache Kafka"
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Mishra
    given-names: Shashank
  - family-names: Mishra
    given-names: Shweta
version: 1.0.1
date-released: 2026-09-13
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/shashank241095/kafka-kg-rag-data"
url: "https://github.com/shashank241095/kafka-kg-rag-data"
abstract: >-
  Frozen research artifacts supporting the manuscript "Evaluating AST-Derived
  Knowledge Graph Retrieval for AIOps Incident Diagnosis in Apache Kafka":
  the audited 315-query benchmark, the archived 321-query benchmark and its
  audit record, the frozen 1,600-record source-linked log corpus, per-query
  retrieval outputs for all evaluated conditions including the ColBERTv2-only
  control and both HippoRAG configurations, downstream evaluation records,
  statistical outputs, configurations, and the pre-specified analysis plan.
keywords:
  - AIOps
  - Apache Kafka
  - knowledge graph
  - graph-augmented retrieval
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - source-code analysis
  - incident diagnosis
  - dense retrieval
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Evaluating AST-Derived Knowledge Graph Retrieval for AIOps Incident Diagnosis in Apache Kafka"
    authors:
